    {
        "desc": "The floor in this part of the wide halls slopes down until it turns into a wide\npool of silvery water. The pool's surface is still and shining like a polished\nmirror, yet deep down it is filled with a faint light. The light seems clearer\nand cleaner than anything you have ever seen. Sometimes it seems the light would\ncome from within of the pool's water itself; these silver reflections are only\nfaint, but still bright and blinding as the highest sun.\n",
